=== DESIGN ===

PIVOT: implement the mount work only (the part of the prompt that is
uncontested) and use the existing FleetTelemetryHandler.Coverage
handler.

D1. Backend (router.go only):
    - Construct fleetTelemetryHandler := NewFleetTelemetryHandler(cfg)
      after L372 alongside other handler constructors.
    - Inside the existing r.Route("/tesla/fleet-telemetry", ...)
      block, mount:
        r.With(httprate.LimitByIP(60, 1*time.Minute)).
          Get("/coverage", fleetTelemetryHandler.Coverage)
      Per-route 60/min rate limit matches the /system/queues precedent
      from Phase-46/41 for read-only admin endpoints.
    - /subscription deliberately NOT mounted (per rubber-duck guidance:
      prompt allows "add 1 route", and the Subscription endpoint can
      be wired in a follow-up if a UI consumer materialises).

D2. Backend test (fleet_telemetry_handler_test.go, NEW):
    Three top-level tests using httptest.NewRecorder + httptest.NewRequest:
    - TestFleetTelemetryCoverage_HappyPath: 200 + sorted categories +
      sorted fields + TotalFields invariant.
    - TestFleetTelemetryCoverage_DestinationTotalsCount: signal_log > 0
      (dual-write counting visible).
    - TestFleetTelemetryCoverage_JSONShapeMatchesFrontendContract:
      asserts every snake_case key the frontend hook depends on is
      present.
    All three are DB-free because the handler is package-derived.

D3. Frontend page (FleetTelemetryCoveragePage.tsx, NEW):
    - PageContainer + summary StatCards row (5 stats: categories,
      routed, subscribed, unsubscribed-but-routed, orphans).
    - Destination breakdown panel — chips sorted by count desc with
      helper text explaining dual-write (also_signal_log) counting:
      "Some fields are dual-written: they appear under their primary
       destination AND signal_log. So signal_log totals can exceed the
       unique routed-fields count."
    - Orphan warning panel renders ONLY when orphan_fields is
      non-empty (rubber-duck guidance).
    - Filter input narrows visible categories.
    - Per-category sections wrap a DataTable with 5 columns: field,
      destination, column, also_signal_log, subscribed.
    - Loading/error/empty/filter-empty states handled.
    - testHookOverride prop for tests (per QueueStatusPanel precedent).
    - Wording: "Routing Coverage", "Package-derived snapshot",
      "Routed, not subscribed". NOT "vehicle coverage", "last seen",
      "24h samples", "coverage_pct" (those would be misleading because
      the handler is package-derived, not telemetry-derived).

D4. Page test (FleetTelemetryCoveragePage.test.tsx, NEW):
    9 tests: loading, categories+stats render, no-orphan-panel-when-empty,
    orphan-panel-when-non-empty, empty state, error banner, filter
    narrows, filter-empty state, refresh triggers refetch.

D5. Mount (App.tsx + Layout.tsx + lazyRoutes.list.ts +
    routePrefetch.ts):
    - App.tsx: lazy import + <Route path="admin/telemetry/coverage" />.
    - Layout.tsx: nav entry in Diagnostics with Icons.cloud +
      text-sky-400.
    - lazyRoutes.list.ts: parity entry near FeedbackQueue.
    - routePrefetch.ts: preloader entry under '/admin/telemetry/coverage'.
    - routeRegistry.ts: regenerated by
      `node web/scripts/generate-route-registry.mjs`.

D6. Hook test fix:
    Change L48 from
      expect(requestMock).toHaveBeenCalledWith('/tesla/fleet-telemetry/coverage')
    to
      expect(requestMock).toHaveBeenCalledWith(
        '/tesla/fleet-telemetry/coverage',
        expect.objectContaining({ signal: expect.any(Object) }),
      )

